| **Rate of Electrophilic Attack** | Alkyl groups on Benzene (Methyl, Ethyl, etc.) | Count \\(\alpha\\)-H. More \\(\alpha\\)-H = Faster reaction. | Using the Inductive effect order (Tert-butyl > Methyl). |
| **Electron Density in Ring** | Comparing Toluene vs. \\(t\\)-Butyl benzene. | Toluene has 3 \\(\alpha\\)-H (\\(+H\\)); \\(t\\)-Butyl has 0 \\(\alpha\\)-H. Toluene is more electron-rich. | Ignoring the number of hydrogens on the \\(\alpha\\)-carbon. |
| **Stability of Alkenes** | Multiple alkyl groups on \\(C=C\\). | More \\(\alpha\\)-H = More HCS = More Stability. | Counting total hydrogens instead of just \\(\alpha\\)-hydrogens. |

